&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California with team members located across the globe. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is expanding its sales footprint and is looking for an Account Executive focused on the DACH region, professional fluency in English and German is required. This remote role can be based anywhere within the UK.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an energetic and motivated sales professional with strong sales skills and channel experience to join our team. The ideal candidate will have 4-8 years of new account or business development experience with a proven track record of engaging the Partner ecosystem to drive success. In your role, you will be responsible for achieving an assigned quota number while also managing lead flow, closing deals, recruiting partners and developing geographical go to market plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective prospecting and lead management building a 3-5X pipeline within your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Predominant focus on closing business in companies with 1000+ employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and reporting a sales pipeline within our CRM, bringing the visibility of the revenue accurately, quarterly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Territory planning and any sales support required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on activities and opportunities delivering short term and long-term revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective and regular networking to attract and influence Partner sales and grow our Partner relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your existing relationships to recruit and onboarding new partners, get them to agree to engage in proactive demand generation activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a regional partner plan mapping partner strengths (customer relationships, vertical focus, technology specialty) to accounts and target opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage lead flow both inbound and outbound between partners and the Bitwarden Sales team. Proactively communicate with Bitwarden sales leaders on the channel pipeline and forecast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with marketing to deliver marketing events/programs/campaigns that create interest and awareness among partners’ customers. Build and execute joint partner business plans with measurable success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set financial goals for focus partners and ensure goals achievement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive multiple key channel initiatives in parallel across technical, professional services, and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-8 years of outside high-tech IT sales experience. IT security product experience is desirable but not mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a startup or pre $100M revenue company is desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track-record of driving continued partner growth and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and strong relationships with SMB and SME focused resellers and MSP partners within a multistate region will be necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive influence and build effective relationships with decision makers across all levels of partner organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated and focused self-starter with strong leadership skills who can multitask, work independently or within a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills including listening, writing and public speaking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can work in a fast paced, start-up environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An avid channel leader who knows how to teach, enable and motivate partners to find and close business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationships and strong relationships with top VARs and Integrators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must demonstrate a consistent track record of achieving annual quota targets while providing specific details on key customer wins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possesses a competitive attitude, strong work ethic and thrives in a fast pace, high growth and matrixed organizational environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive history of collaborative selling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a proficient user of CRM tools and other Gsuite and MS Office tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening call with our Recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with our Head of EMEA Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with our Head of Sales Enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview(s) with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AE Roleplay Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone––from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in a growing market. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow professionally. Embrace the opportunity to build up your demand generation and product-led growth expertise in a fast-growing startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are dedicated to building a diverse and talented team. Work remotely with motivated and supportive team members across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We truly care about our Bitwarden users and want them to have the best experience while accessing their sensitive information online. Our Billing Support team helps people as quickly as possible through our email support system with the majority of inquiries being resolved the same day received. Team members must have excellent writing skills: stellar grammar, attention to detail, and the ability to explain complicated things simply. Success is measured in swiftness, accuracy, and clarity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are searching for an attentive and analytical Billing Support Specialist to assist with resolving billing related customer inquiries, order processing, and account administration. You will advocate for our customers and partner with internal support staff to ensure the client’s specific needs are met to the best of our ability, accounts are billed appropriately, and processes are operating as expected. For this role, we are looking for candidates located in the U.S.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer accounts, generate invoices, collect payments, and update accounts to reflect changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer customer questions about billing and account status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately identify and resolve any billing and account errors or issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review incoming Purchase Orders for accuracy and adherence to sales and finance guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate invoices for new orders as well as renewal invoices and assure they are calculated and recognized correctly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setup and maintain customer accounts in the billing system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with other accounting duties and participate in departmental projects to meet business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for helping Bitwarden users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of empathy and the ability to advocate for others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customer service and communicating billing issues with customers and other internal departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the sensitivity of working with confidential, billing, and accounting information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb organization, attention to detail, and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative problem-solving skills, good judgment, logic, and ability to learn new things quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong work ethic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience multitasking in a cross-functional, fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Google G Suite and/or Microsoft Office applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud and/or web-based applications is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Stripe is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in retail or other fast-paced customer facing environments is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening call with Recruiting Manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Billing Support Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Director&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are dedicated to building a diverse and talented team. Work remotely with motivated and supportive team members across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow. Take on new challenges with the support of your team, and continue personal and professional development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden empowers enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely store and share sensitive data. With a transparent, open-source approach to password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations, Bitwarden makes it easy for users to extend robust security practices across all online activities. Founded in 2016 with headquarters in Santa Barbara, California, Bitwarden is supported by a passionate global community of security experts and enthusiasts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is seeking a dynamic and motivated Channel AE to join our team. This role will focus primarily on fostering partnerships in EMEA. In your role, you will be responsible for managing lead flow, closing deals, recruiting partners and developing geographical go to market plans&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is an all remote team and we&#39;re looking for someone located in the UK who is fluent in either Spanish or Italian and English&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the head of Channel Sales in developing partnerships in EMEA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide quotes and pricing to partners in timely manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the deal registration process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for targeted regions where Bitwarden has taken a channel first strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and cultivate sales leads within targeted regions, feeding these opportunities to resellers as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and nurture relationships with key resellers, enabling them to operate autonomously while ensuring alignment with Bitwarden&#39;s strategic goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver technical and sales training to emerging partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with marketing teams to execute joint marketing efforts that drive brand awareness and sales through channel partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct sales calls with partners and potential customers to support the sales process and provide product expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and nurture relationships with key resellers, enabling them to operate autonomously while ensuring alignment with Bitwarden&#39;s strategic goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a regional partner plan mapping partner strengths (customer relationships, vertical focus, technology specialty) to accounts and target opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent results in a quota based role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of experience in partner development,account management, or channel management,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and maintain strong relationships with resellers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, with a proactive approach to problem-solving and a results-oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage lead flow both inbound and outbound between partners and the Bitwarden Sales team. Proactively communicate with Bitwarden sales leaders on the channel pipeline and forecast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with marketing to deliver marketing events/programs/campaigns that create interest and awareness among partners’ customers. Build and execute joint partner business plans with measurable success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selected candidates will be invited to schedule an introduction call and potentially progress through the following stages:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screening call with our Recruiting Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Hiring Manager (Head of Channel Sales)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with our CSO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with our Head of Sales Enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final Interview with our CEO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reference Checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone––from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in a growing market. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow professionally. Embrace the opportunity to build up your demand generation and product-led growth expertise in a fast-growing startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are dedicated to building a diverse and talented team. Work remotely with motivated and supportive team members across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California with team members located across the globe. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://bitwarden.com&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Channel Marketing Manager to own partner marketing end-to-end — from partner onboarding and enablement to demand generation and events — across MSP, reseller, and VAR motions, prioritizing effort based on revenue potential and business urgency rather than spreading evenly across all three.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an all-remote team and we&#39;re looking for someone located in the U.S. (Preferred East Coast/Central for EMEA support)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Grouped by sequencing, not just importance. This role is expected to partner with leadership to actively triage and prioritize as the programs and opportunities evolve.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the MSP channel marketing motion end-to-end: partner onboarding content, lifecycle email programs, enablement webinar series, and support the annual event calendar (e.g., MSP Summit, IT Nation Connect).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the annual Channel Marketing Plan: event selection, budget, campaign strategy, and executive approval process, in partnership with the Marketing and Sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the marketing primary point of contact for Channel Sales (MSP, reseller, VAR) — running the biweekly Channel Marketing meeting, managing the event intake process, and building/evolving the deliverables (templates, briefs, self-serve assets) that empower Sales to execute quickly and independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own reporting on program performance: pipeline influenced, partner engagement, event ROI, and progress against the $5M combined reseller/MSP revenue target, presented to marketing and sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend proven partner playbooks — onboarding sequences, enablement content, partner toolkits, prioritizing by revenue contribution and need (starting with enabling active partners).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and drive a proactive, always-on partner demand generation strategy to drive net-new target partner interest (e.g., partners in uncovered territories/regions) with a coherent plan tied to pipeline and ARR targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the channel marketing budget across sponsorships, campaigns, and partner enablement programs, and make prioritization trade-offs as new event and partner requests come in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing Operations, Comms, and Product Marketing to keep partner-facing content, campaigns, and the partner portal current and aligned to brand and product roadmap. Wherever possible, focus on public facing web documents that are visible globally by individuals and AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the administration of the Bitwarden partner portal and ensure content is up-to-date, accessible, and aligned with go-to-market priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of B2B channel, partner, or field marketing experience — ideally including work with MSPs, resellers, or VARs in a SaaS or technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to own a marketing program end-to-end: strategy, budget, execution, and reporting, without heavy hands-on direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and executing in-person or virtual partner events, from sponsorship negotiation through post-event lead follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or running partner lifecycle email programs (onboarding, engagement, re-engagement) — comfort partnering with marketing ops/automation owners to execute them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of turning a reactive, request-driven function into a proactive, planned one — you build the calendar instead of just reacting to what lands in your inbox.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills — this role sits at the intersection of Growth Marketing, Channel Sales, and Marketing Operations, and will need trust from all three.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and prioritization — you&#39;ll be handed more inbound requests (events, campaigns, partner asks) than one person can execute, and part of the job is deciding what not to do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and adaptable mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness and authenticity combined with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement and enthusiasm for open source and for better internet security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills – you might not know all the answers, but you know how to find and communicate the solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting with our Recruiting Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with the Head of Growth Marketing and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview(s) with Channel Sales stakeholders (e.g., Channel Sales Manager, Channel Sales AE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview(s) with Growth Marketing team members (e.g., Demand Generation, Product Marketing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with the Chief Customer Officer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reference calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world&#39;s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert. You&#39;ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are dedicated to building a diverse and talented team. Work remotely with motivated and supportive team members across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow. Take on new challenges with the support of your team, and join our #growth-club to continue personal and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California with team members located across the globe. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we establish our India Engineering Center of Excellence (COE), we are looking for an experienced&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; who can lead and grow the Onboarding and Activation team. As the Engineering Manager for the Onboarding and Activation team, you will be expected to lead a team of experienced software engineers responsible for&amp;nbsp;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;the Password Manager user&#39;s journey from first run to paying customer: the onboarding and activation experience that proves the product&#39;s value, and the client-side surfaces that convert it. You&#39;ll ensure that prospective users move smoothly though guided setup, trial initiation, upgrade paywalls and plan selection. For existing users, you&#39;ll manage the user-facing subscription, plan, payment-method, and invoice experiences. This is a critical role for new growth as well as customer retention, where experiences need to be frictionless and error-free.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and retain a strong team of engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and report on measurable goals and objectives for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate team ceremonies including weekly syncs, backlog refinements, retrospectives, and sprint planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor in-flight work to identify blocked items, proactively drive resolution, and provide contextual updates outside of the team to the rest of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own escalation and triage for production issues, community-reported bugs, and enterprise customer escalations related to autofill behavior and desktop integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a healthy, sprint-ready backlog by prioritizing bugs and tech debt alongside feature work and ensuring all items are well-defined with accurate descriptions, technical breakdowns, and designs prior to refinement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary liaison between your engineering team and Design, Product, Architecture, and other engineering teams, fielding cross-functional questions and maintaining alignment on priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the organization to synthesize requests into prioritized, actionable work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously identify friction points in team processes and develop solutions to improve efficiency, quality, and developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an inclusive environment where teamwork and collaboration are valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular 1:1s, develop individualized performance goals and growth plans, and identify stretch opportunities to support each engineer&#39;s career progression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform annual or semi-annual performance reviews when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10-15 years of total experience with 5-8 years of demonstrated experience leading engineering teams or complex cross-functional product engineering initiatives within a software engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in globally distributed Product Engineering, GCC, or Center of Excellence environments along with managing distributed or cross-regional teams, including working across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to successfully lead delivery across engineering organizations and influence multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Agile software development, modern engineering practices, and product delivery lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Engineering Management, Technical Program Management, Engineering Delivery, Product Operations, Design Program Management, or similar leadership roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate effectively with Engineering, Product, Design, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, prioritization, and decision-making skills with a continuous improvement mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A coaching-oriented leadership style with demonstrated experience developing high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background in CI/CD, automation &amp;amp; release engineering - sufficient to engage credibly in technical discussions and step in hands-on when necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with experience representing a team&#39;s work to leadership and stakeholders outside the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience managing or working closely with BRE, SRE, DevOps, or Platform Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formal management training or certifications preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with specific tools like Jira, Confluence, or similar project management platforms preferred with AI tooling for development and workflow support (Claude Code or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success in This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in this position if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead through influence, collaboration, and trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structure without introducing unnecessary processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance strategic thinking with hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clarity across complex, cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy building teams, developing people, and enabling engineering excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
