&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security and IT team at Bitwarden is very active; we work with all teams across the organization every single day. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to contribute to a variety of projects and planning, and will be responsible for managing new and existing security and IT related requests for the business. This role reports directly to the Head of Information Security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an all-remote team, and Eastern U.S. time zone is preferred. We do not offer visa sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with Security and IT related Technical Service Desk tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First touch point for user support (investigation/resolution, referral to TSD/Senior team member, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with access control changes, onboarding automation SCIM, and user provisioning / deprovisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong&lt;/strong&gt; hands-on expertise with configuring and administering/ maintaining Atlassian cloud products (JIRA, Service Management, Confluence, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security and IT administrative tasks related to auditing, access management, and licensing users across various departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responds to, and where appropriate, resolves or escalates security incidents and investigations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist Security and IT and other divisions with ensuring the secure and ethical implementation and operation of AI systems and data within the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigates, monitors and reviews SOC and SIEM alerts and network traffic for unusual or suspicious activity or security events, and investigates these as a first level responder. Provides escalations to tier 2 and tier3 SOC team as needed to assist with investigation of security events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with developing and maintaining documentation for security systems, services and procedures to support Bitwarden’s security, compliance needs and certification requirements such as ISO 27001, SOC2, HIPAA, and GDPR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and maintain endpoint protection and overall security and data protection utilizing various technologies such as Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR), Mobile Device Management (MDM), Secure Access Service Edge (SASE), Data Loss Prevention (DLP), DarkOps and Brand protection service, and other security solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and document standardized processes for managing security and IT services and establish secure/hardened system configuration baselines.&amp;nbsp; Document related IT process and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with patching and updating and overall vulnerability management to keep all systems and endpoint devices secure and operational with minimal downtime.&amp;nbsp; This includes Endpoint/ Asset standardization and maintaining OS and system updates/ patches, leveraging policy enforcements that are managed via our MDM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide security and IT related coverage ahead of the US East Coast time zone. This expands the availability of our security and IT team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Security and IT generalist that has prior experience working in environments with diverse technologies and can dive deep on domain expertise.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing equipment and software across a distributed, remote, and decentralized global workforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain discretion, handle sensitive information and maintain security best-practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interested in solving security and IT challenges through technical awareness, assurance, and partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security technocrat at heart, staying current with trends and new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security standards and regulations relevant to AI and data privacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and adaptable mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness and authenticity combined with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement and enthusiasm for open source and for better internet security&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills – you might not know all the answers but you know how to find and communicate the solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT TO EXPECT IN THE INTERVIEW PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting with our Recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with our Head of Information Security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview/s with team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reference calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A FEW REASONS TO WORK WITH US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are dedicated to building a diverse and talented team. Work remotely with motivated and supportive team members across the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and grow. Take on new challenges with the support of your team, and join our #growth-club to continue personal and professional development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the United States, the starting base compensation range for this role is $115,000 - $145,000. Actual compensation may vary based on level, relevant experience, and skill set as assessed in the interview process, as well as market data by location. See our careers page for a list of benefits. Please note that compensation outside the U.S. will differ based on the market.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://bitwarden.com&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Software Engineer on Bitwarden’s Privileged Access Management (PAM) team, you will lead the design and development of our next-generation privileged access platform. You&#39;ll own critical gateway services, terminal access protocols, and auditing/enforcement at the intersection of security, scalability, and user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In alignment with our modern &lt;strong&gt;True Ownership&lt;/strong&gt; model, our engineers are &quot;T-shaped&quot; professionals who own their services end-to-end—from initial design and secure development to automated testing, deployment, and operational health in production. This role offers unique opportunities to build secure-by-default patterns and make significant contributions to our open-source security ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Support Bitwarden goals by designing, developing, testing, deploying, and operating secure, performant gateway controls, audited terminal logins, and session recording mechanics for our PAM product line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decoupled Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain strict service boundaries and design resilient APIs that allow the PAM platform to operate as an independent, decoupled tenant on our core platform infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Upstream Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely in a co-located, cross-functional &quot;Embedded Trio&quot; (Product, Design, and Engineering) to rapidly design and validate technical solutions prior to code implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automated Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Eliminate manual testing barriers by building and maintaining robust automated test suites, integration harnesses, and CI/CD pipelines for your team&#39;s services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Stewardship:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the operational health, performance, and reliability telemetry of your services in production, proactively participating in sustainable on-call rotations and postmortem analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain high-quality internal architecture specifications, API contracts, and external open-source developer documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall Experience: 8+ years &lt;/strong&gt;as a Lead Software Engineer with team lead experience paired with AI assisted development practices, including experience leading a team&#39;s technical direction, mentoring senior engineers and being accountable for outcomes you did not implement yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with JEST or any other unit testing framework. Set the bar in pull request review and own the team&#39;s conventions for testing, error handling, API design, and secure coding, keeping automated suites, integration harnesses, and CI/CD pipelines strong enough that manual testing is never the safety net. Maintain the architecture specifications, API contracts, and open source developer documentation that go with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Stack:&lt;/strong&gt;Strong proficiency and experience in AI-Led Development in C# / .NET, Rust, or TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience designing or implementing secure gateway architectures, reverse proxies, and session proxying (SSH, RDP, or HTTPS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Auditing:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of Identity and Access Management, key-rotation protocols, and real-time audit logging systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T-Shaped Engineering Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience with containerized environments (Docker/Kubernetes), automated test frameworks (unit, integration, and end-to-end), and SRE/observability tools (APM, alerting, and telemetry dashboards).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Coding:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with zero-trust and zero-knowledge security architectures, encryption standards and threat-modeling methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Spirit:&lt;/strong&gt; A highly collaborative and adaptable mindset, excited to work in rapid, outcome-driven feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Passion:&lt;/strong&gt; Excitement and enthusiasm for open source, developer advocacy, and building a more secure internet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent problem-solving skills—valuing written, clear documentation and using data to make technical decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to play a foundational role in shaping our India Engineering COE from the ground up.&amp;nbsp;Our user community loves us and we love them. Come to work each day with a sense of purpose as we bring a more secure internet experience to everyone from our friends and family to the world’s largest organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Become an expert. You’ll get immersed in the prominent technology markets of security and open source software. You&#39;ll work alongside talented global teams, solve meaningful engineering challenges, influence how we scale our engineering organization &amp;amp; contribute to products used by customers around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building exceptional teams, enabling engineering excellence, and making a lasting impact within a fast-growing engineering company, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can do their best work. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and make employment decisions based on skills, experience, qualifications, and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Bitwarden&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;Bitwarden is the trusted identity security leader for millions of users worldwide, empowering enterprises, developers, and individuals to securely manage and share sensitive information anywhere. Bitwarden makes it easy for all users to extend robust security across their devices with password management, secrets management, and passwordless and passkey innovations. The company is headquartered in Santa Barbara, California with team members located across the globe. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bitwarden.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;bitwarden.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;As a Lead Software Engineer on Bitwarden’s Secrets Manager team, you will lead the design and development of the Secrets Manager application stack that lets developers, DevOps, and cybersecurity teams alike centrally store, manage, and deploy sensitive credentials. You&#39;ll own the core concepts of secrets, projects, machine accounts, and access tokens across the product suite.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;Secrets Manager spans a .&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;NET API, a Rust SDK core, and a TypeScript and Angular web client,&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; with SDK bindings in eight further languages and integrations written in Go, C++, Java, PHP and Python. You should be comfortable moving between languages and learning new ones as the work demands, developing deep expertise as you go.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;This Lead Software Engineer role is &lt;strong&gt;hands-on&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;does not carry any expectations for people management&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll stay close to the code while driving architecture, technical direction, and complex, high-impact engineering problems. As our India Product Engineering organization grows, you&#39;ll help shape its engineering practices and also navigate opportunities to mentor and elevate other engineers through technical leadership.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Delivery &amp;amp; Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, build, test, deploy, and operate secure, performant applications across the Secrets Manager suite. You are accountable for these services end to end, including the parts you did not personally write.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Standards and Automated Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Set the bar in pull request review and own the team&#39;s conventions for testing, error handling, API design, and secure coding, keeping automated suites, integration harnesses, and CI/CD pipelines strong enough that manual testing is never the safety net. Maintain the architecture specifications, API contracts, and open source developer documentation that go with them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decoupled Architecture and Service Boundaries: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain clean service boundaries and design resilient APIs so Secrets Manager can evolve independently of the core platform. Own the medium-term technical direction and record the reasoning behind significant decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Mentorship: &lt;/strong&gt;Grow the engineers around you. Pair on hard problems, give substantive design feedback, and mentor them to grow,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Codebase Health:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to performance, reliability, accessibility, and maintainability. Identify t&lt;em&gt;echnical debt&lt;/em&gt;, articulate its cost, and sequence pragmatic refactoring alongside delivery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Stewardship: &lt;/strong&gt;Own the operational health, performance, and reliability telemetry of your services in production.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership &amp;amp; Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner closely with Product, Design, Security, and the other team&#39;s engineers to design and validate solutions before implementation begins.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO BITWARDEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;8+ years as a Lead Software Engineer with team lead experience paired with AI assisted development practices, including experience leading a team&#39;s technical direction, mentoring senior engineers and being accountable for outcomes you did not implement yourself.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Stack - Expertise:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Expertise in &lt;em&gt;C# / .NET,&lt;/em&gt; with strong working proficiency in &lt;em&gt;Rust&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;TypeScript&lt;/em&gt; / Angular and willingness to build depth in the other. As a lead, you&#39;ll shape how the team adopts AI-assisted development: what gets automated, what stays human-reviewed, and how we hold the quality and provenance bar as output volume rises.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migration Judgement:&lt;/strong&gt; A track record of running incremental modernization inside a live codebase, such as framework upgrades, strict-typing rollouts or state-management migrations, without halting feature delivery or fragmenting the codebase into two competing styles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Stack - Experience&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;Entity Framework with implementations of Postgres, MySQL, and SQLite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;Languages such as Go and Python&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;Tooling such as Terraform, Ansible, and GitHub Actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;Containerized environments such as Kubernetes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;Writing, consuming, and using SDKs / APIs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;AI-assisted development preferable Claude Code&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Stack - Familiarity:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;Languages such as C++, Java, PHP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;WASM instruction format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T-Shaped Engineering Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience with containerized environments (Docker/Kubernetes), automated test frameworks (unit, integration, and end-to-end), and SRE/observability tools (APM, alerting, and telemetry dashboards).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Coding:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with zero-trust and zero-knowledge security architectures, encryption standards, and threat-modeling methodologies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Spirit:&lt;/strong&gt; A highly collaborative and adaptable mindset, excited to work in rapid, outcome-driven feedback loops.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Passion:&lt;/strong&gt; Excitement and enthusiasm for open source, developer advocacy, and building a more secure internet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
